  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` following docs recipe 3. It passes `typecheck`, but I couldn't run it in a browser or run `vite build`, so the scene and the key presses are untested.\n\n- **Scene:** `/assets/soldier.glb` is loaded through `defineModelAssets` with `targetHeight: 1.8`. It stands on a ground plane and plays `Idle` in a loop. A perspective camera frames the whole character. One shadow-casting directional light plus a hemisphere fill light the scene.\n- **Controls:** `R` calls `play(\"Run\", { loop: true, crossFade: 0.4 })` and `I` does the same for `Idle`. Key repeats are ignored.\n- **Eval hooks:** `window.__EVAL__.clip()` returns the target clip as soon as a fade starts. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\nI copied the model's `sha256` from the recipe and couldn't check it against the file here. If it doesn't match the actual `soldier.glb`, the model may not draw.\n\n",
